        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-15T13:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function is called before every draw call to update the immediate constants. So this should be considered hot code. I guess % by a power of 2 constant should be fast.\n\nHowever, it doesn\u0027t make sense to do runtime check on this. This is intended for catching logic bugs only. If it doesn\u0027t satisfy the D3D requirement (constant buffers\u0027 updates\u0027 alignment), the rendering will just appear incorrectly. It shouldn\u0027t cause any security leaks. I think it feels weird to do runtime check on this.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1481,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1481,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "1b216014a2cacc40b6735500ca4afe657c558685",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f497b326_be34ec18",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.cpp",
